  "grammar": {
    "title": "5A: Past tenses - simple, continuous, perfect",
    "explanation": "**worked**, **went**, **ate** are past simple verbs. We use the past simple for finished actions in the past.\n\nFor example, *I *worked* yesterday.* The action is finished.\n\n**was working**, **were playing** are past continuous verbs. We use them for an action in progress at a past time.\n\nFor example, *At ten o'clock, I *was reading*.* The action was in progress.\n\nWe also use the past continuous with **when**. *I was reading when you came in.* The first action was in progress, the second action finished it.\n\n**had gone**, **had finished** are past perfect verbs. We use them for the earlier of two past actions.\n\nFor example, *When I arrived, the ten friends *had gone* home.* They went before I arrived.",
    "examples": [
      "*I *worked* yesterday.* (finished action)",
      "*She *wore* a red dress.* (finished action)",
      "*We *ate* four green apples.* (finished action)",
      "*At ten o'clock, I *was reading*.* (action in progress)",
      "*They *were sitting* on blue chairs.* (action in progress)",
      "*I *was reading* when you came in.* (interrupted action)"
    ],
    "practice": [
      {
        "q": "Did you work yesterday?",
        "a": "Yes, I worked yesterday."
      },
      {
        "q": "What were you doing at ten o'clock?",
        "a": "I was reading."
      },
      {
        "q": "Did she wear a red dress?",
        "a": "Yes, she wore a red dress."
      }
    ],
